  "notes": "{盲信|もうしん} has a negative connotation, suggesting uncritical or naive acceptance of something.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\n- {盲|もう} (blind) + {信|しん} (belief)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {妄信|もうしん}: same meaning, different kanji ({妄|もう} = delusion)\n- {信仰|しんこう}: faith, belief (neutral)\n- {心酔|しんすい}: infatuation, devotion (less negative)\n- {鵜呑|うの}みにする: to swallow whole, believe uncritically\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {盲信|もうしん}してはいけない: one shouldn't blindly believe\n- {盲信|もうしん}{者|しゃ}: a blind believer",
